{"name":"Moonshine","hex":"#c3c2b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moonshine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The light of the moon.\n\nThe light reflected off Earth's Moon.","The light reflected off Earth's Moon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make homemade (especially, illicit) alcohol, especially distilled spirits.","To make (an ingredient) into such a drink."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moonshine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moonshine","blocks":[{"text":"Moonshine is high-proof liquor, traditionally made or distributed illegally. The name was derived from a tradition of distilling the alcohol at night, usually when the moon was out, to avoid detection. In the first decades of the 21st century, commercial distilleries have adopted the term for its outlaw cachet and have begun producing their own legal \"moonshine\", including many novelty flavored varieties, that are said to continue the tradition by using a similar method or locale of production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Himkok.jpg/330px-Himkok.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonshine","wikidata":"Q917046"},{"title":"Moonshine (South Korean TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Moonshine is a South Korean television series starring Yoo Seung-ho, Lee Hye-ri, Byeon Woo-seok, and Kang Mi-na. It tells the story of four young people as they grow up, form friendships and fall in love during the era of strict alcohol prohibition. It aired on KBS2 from December 20, 2021 to February 22, 2022, every Monday and Tuesday at 21:30 (KST) for 16 episodes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2a/When_Flowers_Bloom%2C_I_Think_of_the_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonshine_(South_Korean_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q106813214"}],"images":[{"srcset":"